From: LiveCD Termux maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Permit draining an encoder before its first input picture

Firefox recreates its encoder after draining and drains again until no packets
remain. On an empty encoder pic_end is NULL, but input_order and decode_delay
are both zero, so timestamp adjustment dereferences NULL. No timestamps need
adjusting without a picture. Keep the normal end-of-stream handling below.

--- a/libavcodec/hw_base_encode.c
+++ b/libavcodec/hw_base_encode.c
@@ -504,7 +504,7 @@
 
         // Fix timestamps if we hit end-of-stream before the initial decode
         // delay has elapsed.
-        if (ctx->input_order <= ctx->decode_delay)
+        if (ctx->pic_end && ctx->input_order <= ctx->decode_delay)
             ctx->dts_pts_diff = ctx->pic_end->pts - ctx->first_pts;
     }
 
